==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|peritonaeum}}
* {{alt|en|peritonæum||dated}}

===Etymology===
From {{derived|en|la|peritonaeum}}, from {{derived|en|grc|περιτόναιον}}, from {{mention|grc|περιτόναιος|t=stretched or strained over}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌpɛ.ɹɪ.təˈniː.əm/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-peritoneum.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|peritonea}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} In [[mammal]]s, the [[serous membrane]] lining the cavity of the abdomen and that is folded over the [[viscera]].
# {{lb|en|zoology}} In [[animal]]s, the membrane lining the [[coelom]] cavity.

